1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,725
You'd never expect rocks to move by themselves.

2
00:00:02,745 --> 00:00:04,857
But in Death Valley, they leave trails up

3
00:00:04,877 --> 00:00:07,446
to 100 meters long. What moves them, actually?

4
00:00:07,466 --> 00:00:10,848
In 2013, scientists finally watched it happen.

5
00:00:10,868 --> 00:00:13,175
More than sixty rocks moved at once.

6
00:00:13,195 --> 00:00:15,320
Thin sheets of ice, pushed by light

7
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:17,685
wind, shoved the rocks across the mud.

8
00:00:17,705 --> 00:00:19,771
Not magic. Ice. Solved.

9
00:00:19,791 --> 00:00:21,928
Five more strange places are on the channel.
